PART 5 — COOLDOWNS MUST REMAIN COMPLETELY INTACT

Alva already has a carefully defined cooldown policy.

Do not rewrite it.

The existing policy includes:

* Ordinary repeat cooldown: 0.5 seconds.
* Exceptional ability/effect cooldown: 3 seconds.
* High-impact 10-damage cooldown: 5 seconds.
* Existing exceptions such as Deflect.

Cooldowns depend on the actual move and its mechanics.

The Combo Assist queue must never bypass, shorten, reset, or secretly override a cooldown.

5.1. Source attack cooldown

The original attack’s cooldown must begin according to its existing lifecycle rules.

For a naturally completed ordinary attack, this means when its attack ends.

The queue must not cause the cooldown to start early.

It must not start the source cooldown twice.

5.2. Follow-up attack cooldown

The queued alternate retains its own cooldown.

If it is still cooling down when the original attack finishes, it must not execute.

Do not reset its cooldown to zero.

Do not silently wait several seconds and fire later.

An unavailable queued attack should be discarded at execution time.

5.3. Source and alternate are independent

Example:

Attack 1 finishes.

Attack 1’s 0.5-second repeat cooldown begins.

Attack 2 is ready.

Attack 2 executes.

Attack 1 remains on cooldown.

This is valid.

The cooldown prevents reusing Attack 1 directly; it does not forbid using a different available attack.

Preserve this distinction.

5.4. Do not create a global attack cooldown

Cooldowns are not a universal lock that prohibits all offensive actions.

Do not introduce a global timer between Attack 1 and Attack 2.

The new system must remain compatible with Alva’s existing ability to transition rapidly between different moves.

