PART 7 — PRESERVE ADVANCED ATTACK CANCELLATION

This is a major design priority.

Alva currently allows human players to intentionally cancel their attacks with other valid actions, even without a confirmed hit, subject to the existing rules.

That gives skilled players flexibility and creates a faster combat experience.

Do not remove or unnecessarily restrict this feature.

The new Combo Assist queue must not make manual controls slower.

For example:

Attack 1 → Attack 2

This remains an intentional new-attack request.

The current cancellation rules determine its execution.

Attack 1 → Attack 1

This must never immediately restart Attack 1.

If Combo Assist is enabled and the repeated press occurs inside the queue window, the alternate is scheduled after full animation completion.

Attack 1 → Jump

Keep the existing jump-cancellation behavior.

Attack 1 → Dash

Keep the existing Dash-cancellation behavior and Energy costs.

Attack 1 → Shield

Keep the existing defensive-cancellation behavior.

Attack 1 → Special

Keep the existing eligibility and cooldown rules for that special.

The main distinction is:

Different valid action: preserve deliberate cancellation.

Same active attack repeated: protect the animation and optionally queue a Combo Assist follow-up.

Do not introduce universal animation locks or mandatory recovery delays that would make experienced players feel less responsive.

