PART 22 — NON-NEGOTIABLE ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The assignment is successful only if all of the following are true:

A. Animation safety

Repeated input never restarts, cuts short, or corrupts the current attack animation.

B. Correct sequencing

An accepted queued alternate executes only after the previous attack naturally finishes.

C. Single queue

No button-mashing sequence can pre-schedule multiple attacks from one source animation.

D. Cooldown integrity

Every move continues obeying the established cooldown policy.

E. Manual combat preserved

Direct different-action cancellations remain as responsive as before.

F. Combat Assist compatibility

Queued attacks work correctly with Combat Assist both enabled and disabled.

G. Human-only assistance

CPU fighters never receive the player’s new queued Combo Assist behavior.

H. Cross-device consistency

Keyboard, controllers, and touch controls produce equivalent results.

I. Ground and air correctness

Fighter-specific move mappings and aerial restrictions are respected.

J. Interruption safety

Hits, cancels, landing cancellations, reset and match transitions never leave stale queued attacks.

K. Determinism

Equivalent fixed-step input streams produce equivalent outcomes.

L. Existing balance preserved

Damage, Launch Point, Energy, movement values, attack timing, and CPU intelligence remain unchanged unless an independently verified correctness fix is strictly necessary.

M. Test coverage

All relevant existing and new tests pass, with any environmental exceptions clearly reported.

N. Documentation accuracy

The specification, implementation, and tests agree about how the mechanic works.

